answer_vi:
Generic components cho phép reuse component với nhiều kiểu data. Trong .tsx cần disambiguate `<T,>` hoặc `<T extends unknown>` vì `<T>` bị hiểu là JSX tag. TS 5.4+ thêm `NoInfer<T>` utility để kiểm soát inference tốt hơn.

```typescript
function Select<T>({ options, value, onChange }: {
  options: T[];
  value: T;
  onChange: (v: T) => void;
}) {
  return <select>...</select>;
}
// Dùng:
<Select<User> options={users} value={selected} onChange={setSelected} />
```

answer_en:
Generic components let you reuse a component with multiple data types. In .tsx files you must disambiguate `<T,>` or `<T extends unknown>` because `<T>` is parsed as a JSX tag. TS 5.4+ adds `NoInfer<T>` utility for more control over inference.

```typescript
function Select<T>({ options, value, onChange }: {
  options: T[];
  value: T;
  onChange: (v: T) => void;
}) {
  return <select>...</select>;
}
// Usage:
<Select<User> options={users} value={selected} onChange={setSelected} />
```
